  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Added `heal_tolerance: f64` to `WireRuled` in `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/ruled.rs`, distinct from twist `tolerance`.\n- Validated `heal_tolerance` (`is_finite() && >= 0.0`) at the `wire_contour_ruled` door.\n- Added `UncutRest` and `cover_healed` in `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/laws.rs` using `reach = k + heal_tolerance.max(COVER_TOL)`.\n- Kept `laws::cover` and `laws::cover_run` unchanged for 2-axis, open, and burnout cuts.\n- Updated both `ruled.rs` (uniform widening) and `ruled_widen.rs` (per-ruling widening) to read `cover_healed` on both planes and track the worst rest.\n- Enforced strict `laws::kerf` (`PATH_TOL`) on both lower moves and upper ring moves inside `ruled::emit`.\n- Added an uncut-rest note to `Toolpath::notes` when `COVER_TOL < d - k <= heal_tolerance`.\n- Preserved existing `heal_tolerance == 0.0` refusals byte for byte.\n- Set `heal_tolerance: 0.0` in existing `WireRuled` callers and tests (`operation/wire_ruled.rs`, `wire_4axis.rs`, `ruled_tests.rs`, `wire_fans.rs`).\n- Added `ruled_heal_tests.rs` and `docs/decisions/2693-wire-heal-tolerance.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\n`Region::offset_sharp` already trims local inside-corner swallowtails and bridges shallow slots in 2D.\nHowever, `laws::cover` refused every point past `COVER_TOL` (`0.002 mm`) because `WireRuled` had no explicit healing bound.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pinning tests in `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/ruled_heal_tests.rs`:\n  - `tight_inside_corners_heal_within_heal_tolerance` (failed before fix with `0.0683 mm` cover refusal, passes after fix for `PerRuling` and `Uniform`).\n  - `tight_inside_fillet_heals_within_heal_tolerance` (passes with uncut-rest note, refuses below rest).\n  - `shallow_narrow_slot_heals_within_heal_tolerance` (failed before fix with `0.0600 mm` cover refusal, passes after fix for `PerRuling` and `Uniform`).\n  - `excesses_above_heal_tolerance_refuse_with_spot_depth_and_bound`.\n  - `zero_heal_tolerance_preserves_existing_refusals_and_door_rejects_bad_values`.\n  - `heal_tolerance_stays_distinct_from_twist_tolerance`.\n- Mutation checks:\n  - Disabled door check on `heal_tolerance` in `ruled.rs`: `zero_heal_tolerance_preserves_existing_refusals_and_door_rejects_bad_values` failed; restored and passed.\n  - Reverted `reach` to `strict` in `laws.rs`: four healing tests failed; restored and passed.\n  - Disabled upper bound (`f64::INFINITY`) in `laws.rs`: `excesses_above_heal_tolerance_refuse_with_spot_depth_and_bound` and `tight_inside_fillet_heals_within_heal_tolerance` failed; restored and passed.\n  - Reverted `r.heal_tolerance` to `0.0` in `ruled_widen.rs`: five healing tests failed; restored and passed.\n  - Reverted `r.heal_tolerance` to `0.0` in `ruled.rs`: three Uniform/twist healing tests failed; restored and passed.\n  - Removed the uncut-rest note in `ruled::emit`: three note tests failed; restored and passed.\n- Gate and lint:\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 580 step(s), 0 failed.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed with no warnings.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nnone\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `WireFourAxis`, UI controls, and MCP schemas (covered separately by #2696).\n- Asymmetric XY/UV preimage sewing (#2694) and multi-loop pinch filtering (#2695).\n- Full batch gate and release heavy lanes.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nnone\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: wire: add heal_tolerance on WireRuled to accept bounded 2D inside-corner and slot offsets and report uncut rest\nFixes #2693\n",
